{
  "id": "0e4c21e5-1cf7-4c0a-a00e-76ffbef60703",
  "featureId": "cd083ad1-8310-4368-981b-d14c73c20d96",
  "number": 11,
  "slug": "gridui-10-a-widget-cannot-drop-a-child-s-event-framework-owned-routing-a-self-contained-scrollregion",
  "title": "gridui-10: A widget cannot drop a child's event — framework-owned routing + a self-contained ScrollRegion",
  "status": "planned",
  "discussedAt": "",
  "contextReady": false,
  "contextReadyReason": "",
  "summary": "The framework walks children, not the widget; ScrollRegion owns its whole gesture and reports position through scroll_start/scroll/scroll_end",
  "description": "## The defect, stated once\n\nA `ScrollRegion` mounted in a new surface arrives dead, and nothing fails. It lays out, paints and\nhit-tests perfectly; the wheel does nothing and a thumb drag never ends, so the thumb stays welded\nto the cursor. The user has reported this three times, in three surfaces, and each time it was\nfixed in that one surface.\n\nIt is not a bug in the widget. `ScrollRegion` (heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/scroll_region.rs) already\nimplements the wheel, the thumb drag, the click-in-track page and the press-and-hold repeat, and has\nfor months. The failure is that it is never handed the events:\n\n- `Event::Scroll` never arrives  => the wheel does nothing.\n- `Event::PointerReleased` never arrives => `thumb_grab` is never cleared => the drag never ends.\n\nTwo independent causes, each an omission rather than a mistake:\n\n1. **The host picks a subset.** As of 2026-07-26 `heca/src/app/events.rs` delivered `PointerMoved`\n   + `PointerPressed` to an open modal layer and nothing else; `WindowEvent::MouseWheel` had no\n   modal branch at all; `chrome_dispatch_*` (heca/src/chrome/mod.rs:3108, :3123) has no wheel;\n   `dispatch_pane_header_*` (heca/src/chrome/mod.rs:1193, :1214) has no release. Every seam picked a\n   DIFFERENT subset.\n2. **Each container picks a subset.** `Component::event`'s contract is \"if you override it, you own\n   routing to your children\". 24 widgets override it. `Dialog::event`\n   (heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/dialog.rs:347) carries hand-written arms for `PointerReleased` and\n   `Scroll` whose comments describe exactly these two symptoms — the fix was already written there,\n   which is why it was invisible everywhere else.\n\n## The decision (with the user, 2026-07-26)\n\n**The framework routes to children; a widget only declares what IT does.** Forwarding stops being a\nline anyone writes, so it stops being a line anyone can forget. `Component` loses `fn event` and\ngains `on_event_capture` (before children) + `on_event` (after children), with one free function\n`dispatch(node, ev)` performing the only child walk in the library.\n\nWidgets whose routing genuinely is not a child walk — `Select` (option rows are placed children that\nmust not see input while the list is closed) and `Dialog` (routes through an overlay-aware\n`FocusManager` scan) — keep their current code and declare `routes_own_subtree() -> true` with the\nreason. That is an exception, not a loophole: the pointer-delivery conformance test applies to them\nand fails if they drop a kind.\n\n**`ScrollRegion` is not an exception** — it maps onto the two hooks exactly: capture takes the\npress/thumb-grab and the hover gate (the thumb must beat any child under the cursor), bubble takes\nthe wheel and the release (children first, so the innermost hovered region wins and nesting works\nfor free). The nested-region rule that used to be a comment about calling `route_event` first\nbecomes simply which hook the code sits in.\n\n**Position is reported, never implemented by the caller.** `on_scroll_start` / `on_scroll` /\n`on_scroll_end` carry full browser-shaped metrics (offset_x/offset_y, max_x/max_y, content,\nviewport) plus `Option<&Event>` — `None` means the host's own `scroll_to` moved it, which is what\nlets a scroll-into-view call avoid fighting the user's wheel. A wheel gesture has no natural end, so\n`on_scroll_end` needs an idle timer in `tick`, the same way browsers implement `scrollend`.\n\n## What is already done (2026-07-26, uncommitted, verified green before the trait edit)\n\n- `heca/src/chrome/mod.rs` `dispatch_modal_pointer` — ONE door for pointer events to the modal layer.\n- `heca/src/app/events.rs` — CursorMoved / MouseInput (press AND release) / MouseWheel all route\n  through it; `wheel_event()` maps winit deltas to `Event::Scroll` with the showcase's modifier\n  convention (Shift+wheel = X).\n- `ScrollRegion::release_grabs()` — one definition of \"the gesture is over\", called on release AND\n  on the next press, so a lost release can survive one click, never a session.\n- `heca-grid-ui/tests/pointer_delivery.rs` — the conformance suite (verified to FAIL when Dialog's\n  release arm is removed).\n- `heca/tests/pointer_funnel.rs` — reads the event loop, fails when a pointer branch bypasses the\n  funnel (verified to fail against the pre-fix file).\n\n## In flight / broken right now\n\n`heca-grid-ui/src/component.rs:442` — `fn event` has already been replaced by the two hooks. The 24\nwidgets still define `fn event` and `route_event` still calls `child.event(..)`, so **the workspace\ndoes not compile**. Finishing T1 is what closes that.\n\n## Behaviours that must survive\n\n- Nested regions: the innermost hovered scrollable consumes the wheel; an outer one only scrolls\n  when no descendant did.\n- `bounds === what is drawn === what is clickable` — `sync_shift()` must run before any hit-test.\n- `Select`'s closed rows are zero-sized and must not be clickable; its open panel rect is\n  hit-tested from baked bounds, not tree order.\n- `Dialog`: focus trap, nested overlay first (a Select in the body), scrim dismiss, field-first keys.\n- `ScrollRegion::new()`'s deliberate constructor layout (min sizes Px(0), flex_shrink 1.0,\n  pad_spacing_y, gap_spacing) — a region must be allowed to be smaller than its content.\n\n## Verification\n\nRendering, layout and interaction are verified BY THE USER in the running app, never by green tests\n(memory: no-unverified-rendering-widget-changes). Every interaction this touches — focus traversal,\ndropdowns, context menu, palette, drag-and-drop, sidebar rows, terminal viewport widgets — needs\ndriving before this is called done.",
