    {
      "id": "d3be3b18-5bb2-4670-8468-adbb118988a9",
      "phaseId": "0e4c21e5-1cf7-4c0a-a00e-76ffbef60703",
      "number": 3,
      "shortName": "scrollregion-reports-its-posit",
      "title": "ScrollRegion reports its position — scroll_start / scroll / scroll_end, with full metrics",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "Nobody using a scroll area implements scrolling. This is the other half of that promise: watching it\nmust not require implementing it either.\n\n## Decided with the user (2026-07-26)\n\nThree callbacks, all optional. A host that just wants a working scroll area attaches none.\n\n```rust\npub struct ScrollInfo<'a> {\n    pub offset_x: f32, pub offset_y: f32,   // scrollLeft / scrollTop\n    pub max_x: f32,    pub max_y: f32,      // furthest it can travel\n    pub content: Size,                       // scrollWidth / scrollHeight\n    pub viewport: Size,                      // clientWidth / clientHeight\n    pub event: Option<&'a Event>,            // the wheel/press that moved it; None = host's scroll_to\n}\n```\n\nBorrowed, so no clone on a path that fires at frame rate. The user rejected a synthesized\n`ScrollSource` enum in favour of carrying the real event: `event.is_none()` is exactly \"this was my\nown `scroll_to`\", which is what keeps a scroll-into-view call from fighting the user's wheel.\n\n## Current state\n\n- Half-written and uncommitted (2026-07-26): `ScrollInfo` + a `ScrollSource` enum, an `on_scroll`\n  field/builder, and `set_offset_y` / `set_offset_x` chokepoints that every path now funnels through\n  (wheel scroll_region.rs, thumb drag, `page_toward`, `ensure_visible`, the public `scroll_to*`).\n  **The enum must be replaced by `Option<&Event>` per the decision above.**\n- `scroll_by` gained a source parameter; revisit as the event is threaded instead.\n\n## Build\n\n1. Replace `ScrollSource` with `event: Option<&Event>` on `ScrollInfo`; thread the `&Event` from the\n   handling site into the chokepoint. `scroll_to`/`scroll_to_x`/`ensure_visible`/`scroll_to_child`\n   pass `None`.\n2. Fire `on_scroll` from the chokepoint **only when the value actually changed** (a clamped no-op at\n   either end must not spam).\n3. `on_scroll_start` — the first movement of a gesture. Gesture state exists already for the thumb\n   (`thumb_grab`, `h_thumb_grab`) and the held track press (`track_repeat`); the wheel has none.\n4. `on_scroll_end` — release for thumb/track. **A wheel gesture has no end event**, so it needs an\n   idle timer in `tick(dt)`: fire when nothing has scrolled for ~100ms, which is how browsers\n   implement `scrollend`. `tick` already runs for every layer (heca/src/app/lifecycle.rs:133) and\n   already returns `true` while the track repeat is armed — extend that so a pending scroll-end keeps\n   requesting frames.\n5. All three are `#[host_only(\"behaviour crosses as an Intent, never a callback\")]` for the property\n   macro.\n\n## Edge cases\n\n- **Re-entrancy**: the callback fires inside the mutation. A listener calling `scroll_to` from\n  `on_scroll` either loops or fights the gesture — document it, and consider deferring the fire to\n  the end of the event.\n- The higher-ranked bound (`for<'a> Fn(ScrollInfo<'a>)`) makes the stored closure type uglier than\n  the library's other callbacks; check it stays usable at a call site before committing to it.\n- `max_x`/`max_y` are derivable from `content - viewport`; keep them consistent.\n- A relayout re-clamps both axes (`on_layout`) — decide whether that counts as a scroll (it moves\n  the offset without anyone asking). Leaning yes, with `event: None`.\n\n## Done when\n\n- The three callbacks fire from every path: wheel, thumb, track click, held-track repeat, and the\n  host's own `scroll_to`.\n- Tests: fires on change only; `event.is_some()` for input and `None` for `scroll_to`; the wheel's\n  end arrives after the idle timeout and not before.\n- The USER sees it: `on_scroll_end` firing once at the end of a wheel gesture, not per notch.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\nDONE 2026-07-26 (code + tests; NOT yet driven by the user in the app).\n\n## Shipped — heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/scroll_region.rs\n\n- `ScrollSource` **deleted**. `ScrollInfo<'a>` now carries `offset_x/offset_y`, `max_x/max_y`,\n  `content: Size`, `viewport: Size` and `event: Option<&'a Event>` — the metrics are always present\n  (the user's point: we always have the position), and only the *input* is sometimes absent.\n  `event.is_none()` means the host's own `scroll_to` moved it, which is what stops a scroll-into-view\n  call fighting the user's wheel. Borrowed, so nothing is cloned on a path that fires per frame;\n  `type ScrollListener = Box<dyn for<'a> Fn(ScrollInfo<'a>)>` carries the HRTB.\n- Three optional listeners: `on_scroll_start`, `on_scroll`, `on_scroll_end`, all\n  `#[host_only(..)]` for the property macro.\n- `set_offset_y` / `set_offset_x` remain the single chokepoint every path funnels through (wheel,\n  thumb, track click, held repeat, `ensure_visible`, the public API) and now take the causing\n  `Option<&Event>`. They fire only on an ACTUAL change — a clamped no-op at either end is not a\n  scroll, and there is a test for it.\n- `report_scroll` raises `scroll_start` on the first movement of a gesture; `end_scroll` raises\n  `scroll_end` once and is idempotent.\n- **The wheel's end is a silence.** `WHEEL_IDLE_END = 0.12s`: `report_scroll` arms `wheel_idle` for\n  wheel/programmatic moves, and `tick` counts it down and returns `true` while pending so the host\n  keeps supplying frames — otherwise the timer would only advance when something else redrew and the\n  end would land late or never. A thumb drag and a held track press end on their release instead.\n\nExported as `heca_grid_ui::ScrollInfo` (widgets/mod.rs + lib.rs + prelude).\n\n## Tests (6 new, in scroll_region.rs)\n\n`a_programmatic_scroll_reports_with_no_event`, `a_clamped_no_op_reports_nothing`,\n`the_wheel_reports_with_the_event_that_caused_it`,\n`a_wheel_gesture_ends_after_the_idle_timeout_and_not_before` (also asserts it keeps requesting frames\nwhile pending and stops afterwards), `a_thumb_drag_ends_on_the_release`,\n`the_payload_carries_the_whole_picture`.\n\n933 workspace tests, clippy 0.\n\n## Docs\n\ndocs/widgets.md §ScrollRegion gained \"Using one — the whole surface\": the four-line mount that needs\nno listeners, the three-listener form, a table of what `ScrollInfo` answers, when each fires, and the\nstatement that the host's side is one line.\n\n## Left for the user\n\nDriving it in the app — in particular that `scroll_end` fires ONCE at the end of a wheel gesture\nrather than per notch.",
      "notes": "",
